# /testflight

When Jules-Alexis says `/testflight` (or asks for a TestFlight build after changes):

1. Apply the modifications he just asked for. Follow his instructions. Do not add extra scope.
2. Keep Claude's onboarding/design and Codex's deals/Ask. Do not overwrite a newer deployed `ask-zesty` with older GitHub source.
3. Run `node scripts/check-integration.mjs`.
4. Commit the iOS/app changes on a branch from current `origin/main`.
5. Integrate onto `main` (PR merge or authorized fast-forward) and push. The shared workflow `.github/workflows/testflight_1.yml` only publishes from `main` when `ios-bitewise/**` changes.
6. Confirm the GitHub Actions run succeeds, including archive and upload.
7. Report the exact version/build (e.g. `1.0.0 (YYMMDDHHMM)`), commit, and workflow URL. Upload success is not the same as Apple processing or tester visibility. Do not say testers can install until the build number is confirmed from the workflow.

Do not use extra-cost AI models for this. Do not sync the recipe catalogue to Supabase unless he asks.
